From a3b92ca187404ecfa18264681fca782e1f5814e1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Renaud Breton <renaud.breton@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 10 Aug 2026 15:53:55 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(gr): surface translated editions

- Paginate the GetBook editions query (limit: 100) instead of relying on
  the upstream default page (~20 editions sorted by popularity), which
  effectively hid most non-English editions of popular works.
- Request secondaryContributorEdges in the BookInfo fragment and
  re-attribute translated editions to the work's canonical author when
  the edition's primary contributor is a translator or localized author
  profile but the canonical author is still credited. Previously such
  editions were silently discarded by the controller's author check.
- Extend tests: a translated edition credited to a translator (with the
  author as secondary contributor) is now included and re-attributed;
  a genuinely misattributed edition is still excluded.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
